        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "The plugins route imports `pluginRegistryService`, `pluginLifecycleManager`, `pluginLoader`, etc. — all Node.js-specific services that manage a plugin worker pool. These require filesystem access (`existsSync`, `node:fs`), process spawning (`node:child_process` via plugin-worker-manager), etc.\n\nThe `GET /api/plugins` endpoint would typically return plugins installed on the system — pulled from the DB but enriched with runtime state from the plugin registry (running/stopped status, etc.). These services fundamentally depend on Node.js process management.\n\nSo the current `[]` stub is appropriate for the CF deployment — there's no plugin worker infrastructure in CF Workers.\n\n\nBut I should check whether the handler could at least query the database for installed plugins without needing the runtime state, since that might be feasible even in a serverless environment.",
